    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0360" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.01/199: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase—Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-01-29T17:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29,
                                1924—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 29—4:07
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>29. … This morning I delivered letter to Minister for Foreign Affairs.<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d206-f1"/> He expressed his gratification and stated that
                    similar instructions would be sent to the Greek Chargé in Washington.<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d206-f2"/> …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d206-f1" n="6" xml:id="d206-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 13, Jan. 26, to the Chargé in Greece, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d206-f2" n="7" xml:id="d206-f2-content">
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> from the Greek Chargé presenting
                    his letter of credence to the Secretary of State is dated Feb. 4, 1924 (file no.
                    701.6811/158).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
